WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.567
-Chloe, you look fantastic.
-Why, thank you.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.868
-Thank you so much
for coming back on the show.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.968
The last time I saw you,
you were also very dressed up

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.167
and looking glamorous
and gorgeous.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.567
We were at the Met Gala.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.601
-Oh! I thought you were going
to say at the coffee shop.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:12.701
I'm always --
-Yeah, no.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:13.968
-Yes.

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.067
-We were at the beautiful --
-The beautiful Met Gala.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.300
-And you were doing
a red-carpet thing for Vogue.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.667
-Yes, yes,
I was doing the live stream.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.834
-Have you always been
into fashion?

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.033
-Ever since I was a small child.
-Yeah.

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.000
-I was always, like,
the kid who, like,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.067
I hated wearing jackets.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.901
I hated dressing appropriately.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.901
And my parents would be like,
"You're going to get a cold."

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:36.534
And then my quote was,
"Fashion before death."

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.767
-Wow!
-I was like a 4-year-old.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.000
-I have a picture of you
on Halloween.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.968
This is you in the middle here.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:44.634
-Now, what what costume is this?

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:49.167
-So, I went as a young adult
in kindergarten.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.901
-That was your --
That's what you went as?

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.634
-I really -- I saw this outfit
at JCPenney

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:53.801
and I really wanted it,

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:55.901
and my parents
wouldn't get it for me.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:59.400
And I've been a manipulator
since a small age.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.667
And I was like, "Oh, no,
it's my Halloween costume."

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.167
And they were like --
A little lady.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:06.667
And then trick-or-treating,
they'd be like, "And you are?"

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.467
And I'd be like, "A woman."

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.334
-Your your costume was a woman.
-A woman.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.234
-"That's right. I'm a woman."
Yeah.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.601
You were saying to me
that you --

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.000
With all these fashion things
you're going to --

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.434
Because you're going to
fashion shows.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.901
Have you done an ad
with anyone yet?

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:25.033
-Not yet, Jimmy. I haven't.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.567
-Ooh!
-Gucci.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.234
-Ooh! Gucci!

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:29.367
Why not?
-Why not?

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:30.767
-I think you should be
the face of Gucci.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:34.133
-I should, but I have
to work on my posing.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.501
-What is the problem
with your posing?

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.234
-I don't know
what to do with my hands.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:39.334
Even as we were charading,

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:42.200
I noticed I was, like, standing
in the camera like...

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.300
I have -- I do this thing
called claw hand.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.434
-What is claw hand?

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:49.267
-Every photo I take,
it's like...

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.801
or like...

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.634
-I have -- Oh, yeah,
I have an example here.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:56.067
-Here they go.
-I have three photos of you.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.734
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:01.968
-Very fashion--
very different claw hands.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.100
-Yeah. Yes.
-Now, explain --

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.968
That one I could see.
That's claw hand.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:07.734
-Yeah, that has a pocket.
-Which one? This one does?

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.934
-This had a pocket,
I could have hid my hand,

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:12.200
and, yet, here we are.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.901
-This is fun.
I like -- This is very fun.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.234
-Yeah, so, that was at the VMAs.

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.734
And I clearly don't know
how to hold an object

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.501
with the the claw.

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.534
It's like a lobster.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.701
I did a red carpet once,

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:28.067
and this cameraperson was like,
"Jimmy, give me a thumbs-up."

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.334
And I go, "I don't really do
thumbs-up, you know?"

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:31.934
"Just give me a thumbs-up."

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.434
And I go,
"I don't do thumbs-up."

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.167
"Just come on,
Give me a thumbs-up."

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.767
I go...

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:40.968
And then I was in the
New York Post the next day,

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.934
and it said, "Jimmy Fallon,
give me a weird thumbs-up."

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:44.801
-No!
-It was weird.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.000
It was a little weird.
-It's hard.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.234
-It's not my thing.
-Right.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.133
-My life is hard!
-It's hard!

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:52.901
They think comedy people --
You know, they want you to goof.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.200
They always want me to smile.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.434
-They want the
jokes and the funny.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:57.067
-Yeah. I don't like to
smile in my --

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.534
-You've been joking and
comedying for five years now

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:00.901
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.033
-Yeah, isn't that crazy?
-It's your fifth anniversary.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.634
-A kindergartner.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.501
-So good. You're fantastic.
-Flew by.

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:07.901
-I love you.
-I love you.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.667
-And this week,
you have Pete Davidson.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:11.734
-Yes.
-You have Ice Spice.

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.000
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.334
-Do you get nervous when
you meet the host and the guest?

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:20.033
-Yeah, definitely.
I'm weird with famous people.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:23.033
-You are?
-Yeah. I try and touch them.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:26.133
I don't know. They're --
Like, I didn't grow up in L.A.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:27.434
I don't know.

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:31.300
They're like mythical creatures
to me, the famous.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.300
I saw Jared Leto this summer
and I was like,

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.767
"Oh, my God, Oh, my God."

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:40.167
And I, like, soft-touched his
shoulder without him knowing.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:42.000
-So he didn't know
that you were touching him.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.667
-No, I do it --
No, it's, like, a very --

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.300
-Like, what if I'm here?
-I'd be like...

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.934
And I don't even say hi.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:52.567
I just have to know
that my hand has touched them.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.133
-That is so bizarre.
But that's your thing.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:58.267
-It's normal. It's chill
and cool and totally normal.

00:03:58.267 --> 00:03:59.801
-It's chill and cool
and totally normal?

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:02.801
-Yeah. Yeah.
-I like it. I think it's fun.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:04.968
I think it's a nice thing to do.
-Yeah.

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:08.434
-Well, every time you come on,
I'm very -- Thank you.

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:11.601
-Yes! Sorry.
-It's kind of the claw-ish.

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:12.767
-Yeah, well -- Yeah, they are --

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:13.801
